# Ruling OD-5: `platform-migrate create-first-admin` creates the FIRST admin and refuses once any admin exists. The fault disables the existing-admin refusal in the command; the real binary then
# does not refuse the second run and the harness test must say so. Real Postgres, the real binary (run-db-tests builds it).
GATE=first-admin
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestFirstAdmin_RefusesASecondRunWithTheSameArguments (the command refuses when an admin exists, writes nothing)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestFirstAdmin_RefusesASecondRunWithTheSameArguments$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestFirstAdmin_RefusesASecondRunWithTheSameArguments
